    "summary": "Small clay votive stupa, ts&#039;a-ts&#039;a.  Made of unfired clay pressed from a metal mould and, afterwards, dusted with blue powder paint.  Made up of a central upper dome (spire damaged) with, set on the flanks of the lower part, eight round-domed stupas with staircases.  All of this set on a lotus-petal base.  Below this is a tapering, undecorated element used to extract the moulded part from the mould, and for setting the stupa down on in the shrine.",
